{#
calendar/_toolbar_shell.html.twig — the row above a calendar: where you are, how
to move, and which view.

The fourth shell, and the one with the least in it and the most to get wrong.
Every control is a link, because a view is a URL — each one is bookmarkable, back
works, and the range stays a single indexed query. That is true of the
authenticated calendar and it is true of the public shared page, which has no
session to keep client-side state in even if it wanted one.

**The shell owns the chrome; the caller owns the routing.** This file is handed
finished URLs rather than a route name and parameters, because the two callers
generate quite different ones — `app_calendar_view` with a view and a date, and
`app_shared_calendar_show` with a token in front of them — and a shell that took
a route name would need to know which parameters that route wanted, which is the
whole of the difference between them.

**A step with no URL is drawn as a disabled span, not omitted.** The shared page
publishes a window and its steps run out at the ends of it; drawing nothing there
would change the shape of the row as the reader pages, and moving the date label
under their thumb. The authenticated calendar never passes null — its calendar
has no ends — so the branch costs it nothing, exactly as _month_shell's
"unpublished cell" branch costs it nothing.

`todayUrl` is nullable for a related reason: a shared window need not contain
today, and a "today" button that did nothing would be a control that lies about
what it does. Omitted rather than disabled, because unlike a paging step it is
not part of a row whose shape must stay put.

compact is set by the docked pane. It gets the same four views, as icons rather
than words: the pane is ~380px and "Day Week Month Agenda" spelled out leaves no
room for the date, but dropping the switcher entirely meant the pane could only
ever show its agenda — there was no way to reach the month from it at all.

Variables:
  view       CalendarView  which one is current
  anchor     date          what the label is built from
  rangeFrom  date          the visible range's first instant, for the week label
  rangeTo    date          its exclusive end
  prevUrl    string|null   null draws a disabled span
  nextUrl    string|null   likewise
  todayUrl   string|null   null renders no button at all
  viewUrls   map           view value => URL; a value that is absent is not
                           offered, which no caller does today and which is the
                           honest way to offer three of them one day
  compact    bool          optional, icons instead of words
  frame      string|null   optional, a Turbo Frame every link targets
  spanLabel  bool          optional, label the range rather than the anchor.
                           Defaults to true for week and false for everything
                           else, which is what each view means by "where you
                           are": a week IS a range, a month is named by its name,
                           and a day is a day. The shared calendar's agenda
                           passes true — it is a bounded page of the published
                           window rather than the authenticated agenda's rolling
                           list from a date, so its two ends are the honest label

Blocks:
  toolbar_actions  the right-hand end, after the switcher
#}

{% set compact = compact|default(false) %}
{% set frame = frame|default(null) %}
{% set spanLabel = spanLabel|default(view.value == 'week') %}

{% set viewIcons = {
    day:    'fa-calendar-day',
    week:   'fa-calendar-week',
    month:  'fa-calendar-days',
    agenda: 'fa-list-ul',
} %}

<div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 border-b border-line shrink-0 min-h-[var(--pane-header-h)]">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-0.5 shrink-0">
        {% if prevUrl is not null %}
            <a href="{{ prevUrl }}"
               {% if frame %}data-turbo-frame="{{ frame }}"{% endif %}
               class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors"
               aria-label="{{ 'calendar.nav.previous'|trans }}"
            ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-left text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
        {% else %}
            <span class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-faint opacity-40"
                  aria-hidden="true"
            ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-left text-xs"></i></span>
        {% endif %}

        {% if todayUrl is not null %}
            <a href="{{ todayUrl }}"
               {% if frame %}data-turbo-frame="{{ frame }}"{% endif %}
               class="px-2 h-7 flex items-center rounded-lg text-xs text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors"
            >{{ 'calendar.today'|trans }}</a>
        {% endif %}

        {% if nextUrl is not null %}
            <a href="{{ nextUrl }}"
               {% if frame %}data-turbo-frame="{{ frame }}"{% endif %}
               class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors"
               aria-label="{{ 'calendar.nav.next'|trans }}"
            ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
        {% else %}
            <span class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-faint opacity-40"
                  aria-hidden="true"
            ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right text-xs"></i></span>
        {% endif %}
    </div>

    {# A week is a range, and saying "1 Aug 2026" over a grid running 27 Jul to
       2 Aug is just wrong. The year is dropped from the near end when both ends
       share it, and the month too when the week does not cross one.

       **`false` on every date filter below, and it is load-bearing.** These
       three values were built in the calendar's OWN zone — by
       CalendarRangeReader for the owner's calendar and by
       SharedCalendarRangeBuilder for a shared one — and `false` is what tells
       Twig to format them there instead of converting them to its default
       first. Without it a Berlin calendar's month anchor, which is midnight on
       the 1st, is re-read as 22:00 on the 31st wherever the default is UTC, and
       the toolbar over an August grid says July. The authenticated calendar
       never showed it, because TwigTimezoneSubscriber makes the default the
       user's own zone and the conversion is then a no-op; a page with no user
       has no such luck, which is how it was found. #}
    <h2 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink truncate min-w-0" data-calendar-position>
        {%- if spanLabel -%}
            {% set spanStart = rangeFrom %}
            {% set spanEnd = rangeTo|date_modify('-1 day') %}
            {{ spanStart|date(spanStart|date('Y', false) == spanEnd|date('Y', false)
                ? (spanStart|date('n', false) == spanEnd|date('n', false) ? 'j' : 'j M')
                : 'j M Y', false) }}
            – {{ spanEnd|date('j M Y', false) }}
        {%- elseif view.value == 'month' -%}
            {{ anchor|date('F Y', false) }}
        {%- else -%}
            {{ anchor|date('j M Y', false) }}
        {%- endif -%}
    </h2>

    <div class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-1 shrink-0">
        <div class="flex items-center rounded-lg border border-line overflow-hidden" data-calendar-views>
            {% for candidate in enum('App\\Domain\\Enum\\Calendar\\CalendarView').cases() %}
                {% if viewUrls[candidate.value] is defined %}
                    {% set label = ('calendar.view.' ~ candidate.value)|trans %}
                    <a href="{{ viewUrls[candidate.value] }}"
                       {% if frame %}data-turbo-frame="{{ frame }}"{% endif %}
                       aria-current="{{ candidate == view ? 'page' : 'false' }}"
                       {% if compact %}aria-label="{{ label }}" title="{{ label }}"{% endif %}
                       class="flex items-center justify-center text-xs transition-colors
                              {{ compact ? 'w-7 h-7' : 'px-2.5 py-1' }}
                              {{ candidate == view ? 'bg-accent text-accent-ink' : 'text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink' }}"
                    >
                        {%- if compact -%}
                            <i class="fa-solid {{ viewIcons[candidate.value] }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        {%- else -%}
                            {{ label }}
                        {%- endif -%}
                    </a>
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
        </div>

        {% block toolbar_actions %}{% endblock %}
    </div>
</div>
